## CREATING NEW ERC-3643 POOLS ON DCSWAP

To list an ERC-3643 security token on DCSwap:

### Step 1: Deploy the ERC-3643 Token

**NOTE:** T-REX/ONCHAINID contracts must be redeployed first. The addresses below are placeholders — use the actual deployed addresses from the T-REX redeployment.

```javascript
const { ethers } = require("ethers");
const provider = new ethers.JsonRpcProvider("https://erpc.datachain.network", { chainId: 271828 });

// Deploy ModularCompliance
const compliance = await deployContract(deployer, ModularCompliance, []);
await compliance.init();

// Deploy Token
const token = await deployContract(deployer, Token, []);
await token.init(
  IDENTITY_REGISTRY_ADDRESS, // from T-REX redeployment
  compliance.address,
  "Token Name", "SYMBOL", 18,
  deployerONCHAINID  // owner identity
);

// Bind, mint, unpause
await compliance.bindToken(token.address);
await token.addAgent(deployer.address);
await token.mint(deployer.address, ethers.parseEther("1000000"));
await token.unpause();
```

### Step 2: Register DEX Infrastructure in T-REX

The DCSwapRouter and the new pool must be registered as verified identities in the IdentityRegistry so ERC-3643 transfer checks pass:

```javascript
const identityABI = require("@onchain-id/solidity/artifacts/contracts/Identity.sol/Identity.json").abi;
const proxyArt = require("@onchain-id/solidity/artifacts/contracts/proxy/IdentityProxy.sol/IdentityProxy.json");

// Deploy identity proxy for Router (deployer-managed)
const routerProxy = await new ethers.ContractFactory(proxyArt.abi, proxyArt.bytecode, deployer)
  .deploy(IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORITY_ADDRESS, deployer.address); // from T-REX redeployment
const routerOID = await routerProxy.getAddress();

// Add CLAIM key for DatawalletClaimIssuer
const oid = new ethers.Contract(routerOID, identityABI, deployer);
const keyHash = ethers.keccak256(ethers.AbiCoder.defaultAbiCoder().encode(
  ["address"], [CLAIM_ISSUER_ADDRESS] // from T-REX redeployment
));
await oid.addKey(keyHash, 3, 1);

// Register in IdentityRegistry
const idReg = new ethers.Contract(IDENTITY_REGISTRY_ADDRESS, [...], deployer);
await idReg.registerIdentity(
  "0x8ebdd966e9e9af2ec5d02c886b1c4b5ba617e7c4", // DCSwapRouter (current)
  routerOID,
  250 // country code
);

// Issue claims via DatawalletClaimIssuer for ALL 6 topics
const issuer = new ethers.Contract(CLAIM_ISSUER_ADDRESS, [...], deployer);
for (const topic of [1, 2, 3, 4, 10, 99]) {
  await issuer.issueClaimToIdentity(routerOID, topic, claimData);
}

// Repeat for the pool address after creation
```

### Step 3: Create Pool on DCSwap

```javascript
const FACTORY = "0x772e5fd559069aecce5e6983c0c415c8579d780d";
const ROUTER  = "0x8ebdd966e9e9af2ec5d02c886b1c4b5ba617e7c4";
const WFAT    = "0x285eecf51d5f0a6ab8d8151139b4d19b05c6b3e4";

const factory = new ethers.Contract(FACTORY, FACTORY_ABI, deployer);
const router  = new ethers.Contract(ROUTER, ROUTER_ABI, deployer);

// Create pair
await factory.createPair(tokenAddress, WFAT);
const pairAddr = await factory.getPair(tokenAddress, WFAT);

// Approve and add liquidity
await tokenContract.approve(ROUTER, ethers.MaxUint256);
await router.addLiquidityFAT(tokenAddress, tokenAmount, tokenMin, fatMin, deployer.address, deadline, { value: fatAmount });
```

